{
  "version": "1.19.0",
  "organization": "ScaleDock",
  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Create, upgrade or align ScaleDock product, library and tooling repos against one standard: the latest Node that Vercel supports, latest pnpm and the stable native TypeScript compiler, a strict Turborepo workspace, Next.js surfaces or a universal Expo app, an optional native-only Expo mobile app with PowerSync for offline data, Supabase with better-supabase (a local project per worktree or agent on the native runtime with no container engine, test databases on that stack, and declarative schemas on pg-delta), Stripe Data Pipeline for billing reads, PermDock, an oRPC contract shared by the API, MCP and CLI, Fumadocs, and a library profile (a structural Instant, Standard Schema only, tested peer floors and a TypeScript matrix), and Vercel-first infrastructure (Vercel Flags, Workflow SDK 5, the Run SDK and Sandbox with Drives, Connect for third-party tokens, and Services with bindings). AI features use AI SDK 7 through AI Gateway, with `WorkflowAgent` for long runs, declared tool approvals and shadcn AI Elements; Next.js 16.4 routes guard their static output with `ensureStatic`. Lint and format run on Ultracite 8 over Oxlint and Oxfmt with type-aware rules at error, JSDoc formatting and collapsed objects; toolchain bumps land as their own reformat commit, and disabled rules come back group by group with a written keep-off list and re-measured counts. A TypeScript minor in pre-release is prepared for but never installed, with its known breaks (such as 7.1 distributed conditional types) fixed ahead and a pending upgrade checklist in AGENTS.md; CI uses each action's latest major tag with zizmor ref-pin and a Dependabot cooldown, runs the cheap gates as parallel steps in one job and the heavy ones as separate jobs, builds first where the measured chain allows, skips heavy suites that `turbo query affected` says a change cannot reach, selects task entrypoints strictly so test jobs stop building unrelated Next.js apps, saves caches only from the default branch, scopes cache access with cache-mode, and runs zizmor on public repos, Valibot covers every schema, and Temporal is the one date library. Every CLI follows the contract better-supabase and PermDock share: a static command manifest with side effects, a `cli-result-v1` JSON envelope, exit 3 for action required, an agent mode with consent tokens, one file-write plan, stdin secrets and completion; scaffolding CLIs keep their web builder, `init` flags and generated config in parity from one catalogue. Runs record bundle, type and CLI-startup baselines before and after, agent routes are cached, and every adapter shares one naming scheme that a drift test enforces. Every Next.js surface (app, docs and marketing) follows the `nextjs-app-architecture` skill, and one shared web design reference gives the three the same section layouts, sidebar shell and scrolling, copy button, theme shortcut, URL-backed tabs that work on prerendered pages, lazy heavy client code, accessible server-rendered diagrams, tested icon and integration maps, and Markdown mirrors. Agents verify Next.js work through the dev server's MCP endpoint and keep the tool-managed AGENTS.md blocks committed. Upgrade and align modes fill a gap table from a fixed checklist with a fixed status vocabulary, and every run ends with a report template; every version is looked up at run time. SKILL.md holds the inputs, ground rules, workflow and final checklist, and each area of the standard lives in its own reference so the agent loads only what the repo kind and selected surfaces need.",
